# A way a permanent grants to cast from the graveyard (CR 601.3, 118.9) is judged on the face being cast: casting a Room is choosing a door
# (CR 709.3), only that door's characteristics are considered ("you could cast Bottomless Pool this way, but not Locker Room"), and that door
# is the one unlocked as it enters (CR 709.5d). Serra Paragon casts Unholy Annex ({2}{B}, mana value 3), not Ritual Chamber ({3}{B}{B}); the
# cast names the door: Cast(Ability: Unholy Annex: Once during each of your turns).
# Bot1 casts Unholy Annex on turn 1, Serra Paragon the same turn, on turn 3 Disenchants its own Room, and on turn 5 casts Unholy Annex from the
# graveyard with the Paragon's permission; it enters with Annex's door unlocked, exiled if it dies (the Paragon's gift).

